</section><section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwAtk" aria-labelledby="Products"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Products">Products</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rolls-Royce_Holdings&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21" title="Edit section: Products"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAto"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Olympus_593_AB.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAts"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Olympus_593_AB.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Olympus_593_AB.jpg/250px-Olympus_593_AB.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3307" data-file-height="2020" data-file-type="bitmap" height="153" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Olympus_593_AB.jpg/500px-Olympus_593_AB.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAtw"/></a><figcaption id="mwAt0">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce/Snecma_Olympus_593" title="Rolls-Royce/Snecma Olympus 593" id="mwAt4">Olympus 593</a> powered the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concorde" title="Concorde" id="mwAt8">Concorde</a> supersonic transport.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAuA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Conway_RCo_17_(26856340848).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAuE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Conway_RCo_17_(26856340848).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Conway_RCo_17_%2826856340848%29.jpg/250px-Conway_RCo_17_%2826856340848%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3847" data-file-height="2695" data-file-type="bitmap" height="175" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Conway_RCo_17_%2826856340848%29.jpg/500px-Conway_RCo_17_%2826856340848%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAuI"/></a><figcaption id="mwAuM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Conway" title="Rolls-Royce Conway" id="mwAuQ">Conway</a> was the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbofan" title="Turbofan" id="mwAuU">turbofan</a> to enter service.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAuY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bristol_Siddeley_Pegasus_(28135065767).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAuc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bristol_Siddeley_Pegasus_(28135065767).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Bristol_Siddeley_Pegasus_%2828135065767%29.jpg/250px-Bristol_Siddeley_Pegasus_%2828135065767%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="6000" data-file-height="4000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Bristol_Siddeley_Pegasus_%2828135065767%29.jpg/500px-Bristol_Siddeley_Pegasus_%2828135065767%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAug"/></a><figcaption id="mwAuk">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Pegasus" title="Rolls-Royce Pegasus" id="mwAuo">Pegasus</a> with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thrust_vectoring" title="Thrust vectoring" id="mwAus">vectored thrust</a> for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harrier_jump_jet" title="Harrier jump jet" id="mwAuw">Harrier jump jet</a></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAu0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rolls-Royce_Trent_XWB_Fan,_ILA_2018.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAu4"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rolls-Royce_Trent_XWB_Fan,_ILA_2018.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Rolls-Royce_Trent_XWB_Fan%2C_ILA_2018.jpg/250px-Rolls-Royce_Trent_XWB_Fan%2C_ILA_2018.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4141" data-file-height="4175" data-file-type="bitmap" height="252" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Rolls-Royce_Trent_XWB_Fan%2C_ILA_2018.jpg/500px-Rolls-Royce_Trent_XWB_Fan%2C_ILA_2018.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAu8"/></a><figcaption id="mwAvA">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A350" title="A350" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvE">A350</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trent_XWB" title="Trent XWB" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvI">Trent XWB</a> is Rolls-Royce largest engine.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAvM">Rolls-Royce's aerospace business makes commercial and military <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_turbine" title="Gas turbine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvQ">gas turbine</a> engines for military, civil, and corporate aircraft customers worldwide. In the United States, the company makes engines for regional and corporate jets, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helicopter" title="Helicopter" id="mwAvU">helicopters</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turboprop" title="Turboprop" id="mwAvY">turboprop</a> aircraft. Rolls-Royce also constructs and installs power <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrical_generator" title="Electrical generator" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvc">generation</a> systems. Its core gas turbine technology has created one of the broadest product ranges of aero-engines in the world, with 50,000 engines in service with 500 airlines, 2,400 corporate and utility operators and more than 100 armed forces, powering both <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fixed-wing_aircraft" title="Fixed-wing aircraft" id="mwAvg">fixed-</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helicopter" title="Helicopter" id="mwAvk">rotary-wing aircraft</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Marine_Power_Operations" title="Rolls-Royce Marine Power Operations" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvo">Rolls-Royce Marine Power Operations</a> (a subsidiary company) manufactures and tests <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_reactor" title="Nuclear reactor" id="mwAvs">nuclear reactors</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Navy" title="Royal Navy" id="mwAvw">Royal Naval</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submarines" title="Submarines" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAv0">submarines</a>.<sup about="#mwt315" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-95" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-95"}}'><a href="#cite_note-95" id="mwAv4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAv8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwA">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwAwI" aria-labelledby="Aerospace"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Aerospace">Aerospace</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rolls-Royce_Holdings&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22" title="Edit section: Aerospace"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

