<ul id="mwB8U"><li id="mwB8Y">1906 company, <b id="mwB8c">Rolls-Royce Limited</b>. Its shares became more or less valueless in 1971 and their price sank as low as a penny from a high of £1.25.</li></ul>
<dl id="mwB8g"><dd id="mwB8k">By the time the liquidation was effectively complete those shareholders had received more than £0.60 per share from the liquidation and they may have bought them for around a penny.</dd></dl>
<ul id="mwB8o"><li id="mwB8s">1971 company, floated as <b id="mwB8w">Rolls-Royce plc</b> still owns the principal business but itself was sold to the new holding company in 2003</li>
<li id="mwB80">2003 company floated as <b id="mwB84">Rolls-Royce Group plc</b> bought the 1971 company</li>
<li id="mwB88">2011 company floated as <b id="mwB9A">Rolls-Royce Holdings plc</b> bought the 1971 company from the 2003 company</li></ul></span></li>
</ol></div></div>

